## 5. Guardrails worth adding

**Startup validation** – fail fast if a handler is misconfigured:

```java
@Component
@RequiredArgsConstructor
public class HandlerValidator implements ApplicationRunner {
    private final TopicHandlerRegistry registry;
    @Override public void run(ApplicationArguments args) {
        if (registry.all().isEmpty()) throw new IllegalStateException("No TopicHandler beans found – nothing to consume");
        registry.all().forEach(h -> Assert.hasText(h.topic(), h.getClass() + " has empty topic()"));
    }
}
```

**Per-handler metrics tag** – tag with the flow type so dashboards show "redis-lookup vs direct-api" behaviour:

```java
default String flowType() { return getClass().getSimpleName(); }
// in pipeline: tags.and("flow", handler.flowType())
```

**Per-handler timeout** – a Redis-scanning flow may need more time than a direct API call:

```java
default Duration processingTimeout() { return null; }   // null → app.processing.timeout
// pipeline: .timeout(Optional.ofNullable(handler.processingTimeout()).orElse(props.processing().timeout()))
```

