### Resulting layering

```
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  Kafka ingestion pipeline  (generic: receive → deserialize →  │
│  handle → ack/DLT; one KafkaReceiver + group per topic)       │
├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│  TopicHandler<T>  (contract: topic, payloadType, handle)      │
├───────────────┬───────────────┬───────────────┬──────────────┤
│ NationalCode  │ DirectApi     │ RedisWriter   │ Forwarding / │
│ LookupHandler │ Handler       │ Handler       │ Step chains  │
├───────────────┴───────────────┴───────────────┴──────────────┤
│  Ports: NationalCodeLookup, ResilientApiClient, KafkaSender,  │
│  ReactiveStringRedisTemplate                                  │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

Adding a new business is still **one `@Component`** — you just choose which row of the third layer it sits on. The Redis lookup is now an opt-in capability rather than something every topic pays for.